    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41261" root="هلب" body-key="h">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُلْبَةٌ</span></b>  The <i>hair that is above the pubes, extending near to the navel.</i> (TA.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُلْبٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُلْبَةٌ</span> <i>Severity,</i> or <i>pressure,</i> of fortune: like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُلْبَةٌ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُلْبَةٌ</span>. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُلُبَّةٌ</span></b> , <i>Severity,</i>
or <i>intenseness,</i> of winter. (K.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتَيْتُهُ فِى هلبةِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الشِّتَاءِ</span> <i>I came to him during the severe,</i> or <i>intense,
cold of winter.</i> (El-Umawee.)

